          %title Arity spaces
          %h1#arity_spaces Arity spaces
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %li
                %a{:href => "#construction_as_a_comma_double_category"} Construction as a Comma Double Category
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %strong arity space
            is a common generalization of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+spaces"} coherence spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finiteness+spaces"} finiteness spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totality+spaces"} totality spaces
            to an arbitrary set of “arities”.
          .standout
            %p
              This is an original and tentative definition. In particular, it’s not clear whether the allowed sets of arities should be restricted in some way. Should they be an
              = succeed "?" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arity+class"} arity class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
              (coherence spaces),
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1,2,3,\dots\}
              (finiteness spaces), and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{1\}
              (totality spaces), which are all arity classes.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            be a set of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinal+numbers"} cardinal numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ,
                  %mi v
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u,v\subseteq X
            of the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\perp v
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |u\cap v|\in \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+connection"} Galois connection
            in the usual way: for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒰
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}\subseteq P(X)
            we have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mo ⊥
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo .
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}^\perp = \{ v \mid \forall u\in \mathcal{U}. u\perp v \}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \perp
            is symmetric,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\perp
            is self-adjoint on the right.
          %p
            We define a
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              \-arity space
            to be a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            together with a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒰
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}\subseteq P(X)
            that is a fixed point of this Galois connection,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mo ⊥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U} = \mathcal{U}^{\perp\perp}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              \-ary
            and the sets in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}^{\perp}
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                co-
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                \-ary
          %p
            A
            %strong morphism
            or
            %strong relation
            between
            = succeed "-arity" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mi ⇸
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R: X &amp;#8696; Y
            such that
          %ol
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\subseteq X
              is
              = succeed "-ary," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
